{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1364705-switching-paths","id":1364705,"title":"Switching Paths?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-01T23:29:39-08:00","id":1364705,"title":"Switching Paths?","content":"I can't seem to find in the books anything about how to switch Paths in-game due to character development and how that should be handled mechanically. I know there are Conditions for when you screw up with a Path, but I'd like to know what happens when you leave a Path entirely and start on another (sometimes from scratch). Fiction is filled with such stories, for example the violent character who, during the course of a season of games, starts to renounce their violent ways and become a monk. Or the materialistic millionaire who gets fed up with their existence, sells everything and lives a simple life as a hippie. Or a person working for a major organization who switches sides and starts to advance in another.<br /> <br /> What's the best way to handle such cases, mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T03:21:51-08:00","id":1364728,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t switch path, but you can have more than 3 paths. The people you used to know are still there and the things you had too, as well as all you learned.<br /> <br /> If you abandoned the previous path, for example becoming a traitor or left the company you can suggest get the condition Path Suspension or even Path Revoked (Core page 41). That way you lose the path uses, but keep the characteristics granted by the path dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T09:23:43-08:00","id":1364774,"title":"","content":"The 'best' way is to swap you old path with a new path that grants you the same Skills and Edges that you'd already taken with your old path, and claim you've slowly become estranged from your old connections while forming new ones. Swap the name of the path and you're done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This can be easy since you are allowed to design your own paths, and you can be fairly liberal in the skills and edges you choose to include.<br /> <br /> As an easy example, say you want to play a variant Aberrant game in the My Hero Academia setting. If you really want to get into the feel of the setting, you'd start as a UA applicant, go on to become a UA student, then graduate to become a professional Hero. You could create a UA Hero Aspirant Role or Society Path for taking the entry test, adjust it into a UA Hero Student Role/Society Path when you get in, then adjust it to a UA Graduate Role/Society Path when you graduate.<br /> <br /> For a less direct example, have your former cop character become a criminal, but claim he's using the skills and edges he learned as a cop to flourish in his new role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T10:51:13-08:00","id":1364788,"title":"","content":"Thank you for some good and informative answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}